= Medieval History

The Middle Ages span from the 5th to the 15th century in Europe.
Feudalism defined the social and political structure of this long era.
Knights and castles were central institutions of medieval warfare.

The Black Death devastated Europe throughout the 14th century.
Approximately one-third of the entire population perished from the plague.
This demographic catastrophe fundamentally reshaped European society.

The Renaissance began in Italy during the 14th and 15th centuries.
A renewed interest in classical antiquity drove artistic and intellectual change.
